lines? I never thought of it before since I'm a guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outstar said that Damsel was there to recruit for the Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T21:53:50-07:00","id":1455901,"title":"","content":"I wanted a useful ghoul with skills. Heather was a liability, and I resent the way sex appeal is misused in this game. I'd like to think the pc picks up mercucio after the story ends.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought Damsel and Nines were joke characters. Couldn't take either of them seriously. Damsel felt very deliberate (&quot;it'd be like communism but it'd actually work!&quot;) and, well, Nines isn't much better. Don't understand the other characters acting like he's charismatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T22:18:22-07:00","id":1455903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455885#post1455885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think a more effective Anarch character to reintroduce, would be Nines Rodriguez primarily. Damsel.. I don't think she's even much a fan favorite. The most popular female characters (though of course, is not objective, just me parsing the minutiae fandom surrounding VTM:B) in Bloodlines was Therese/Jeanette Morgan, Heather Poe because she's the one and only Ghoul you can have, followed by Velvet for the type of sexy attire she wears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nines and the Voermans are major supporting characters in the L.A. by Night podcast, so they probably wanted to avoid contradicting anything they establish there. And I get the impression that Damsel is pretty fondly-remembered - she's one of the commentators in BJD, too. So there's precedent.<br /> <br /> Damsel was one of my favourite Bloodlines characters back as a first-time player. She was one of the few major female characters in Bloodlines who wasn't sexualised (I pretend the poster sidequest never happened), and the comical hostility and vocal resemblance to Francine from <i>Arthur</i> also made it entertaining to interact with her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually speaking of Heather, did any of the female users on this site ever want a male Ghoul option in Bloodlines? I never thought of it before since I'm a guy. </div> </div> </div>Probably. Male blood dolls would have been nice, too. That's mostly in hindsight, though. Weirdly, &quot;horny teenage boy&quot; being the default assumed audience for video games was so common that you stopped noticing it pretty quickly and just latched onto the exceptions, like the Romero sidequest... or quelle horreur, Chunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26959-tofana-by-l-oreal","user":"Tofana by L'Oreal","date":".  EDIT: just a Chunk-a-Chunk-a-burnin'-love 08-01-2021, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26959-tofana-by-l-oreal","name":"Tofana by L'Oreal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T00:38:36-07:00","id":1455905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455901#post1455901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted a useful ghoul with skills. Heather was a liability, and I resent the way sex appeal is misused in this game. I'd like to think the pc picks up mercucio after the story ends.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought Damsel and Nines were joke characters. Couldn't take either of them seriously. Damsel felt very deliberate (&quot;it'd be like communism but it'd actually work!&quot;) and, well, Nines isn't much better. Don't understand the other characters acting like he's charismatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked Damsel but yeah, mainly because she was a fun character. Most of the characters in Bloodlines tended to be fairly serious. Damsel was so over the top serious and hardcore she wrapped over to goofy, which was clearly the intent. I think that was true for most of the Anarchs where you got a sense of dramatic irony. But then that's always been the case with the Anarchs in Vampire. They who tend to talk a big game about freedom and all that, but really all they want is a turn in the big chair. The reality is, in Anarch Territory, the new boss usually isn't much different from the old boss (oh no we don't have a <i>Prince</i>, we have a <i>Baron.</i>). At least Smiling Jack was cool.<br /> <br /> As for Heather, I thought she was great. You got to see her addiction to your blood as the game went one, where she leaves her apartment to stay with you. And then pulls out all of the money she was saving for college to give to you. Most of the ghouls in the game feel a little bit off, as they should, but I thought they did a really good job with showing how off ghouls can quickly get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-01-2021, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T00:51:42-07:00","id":1455909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455885#post1455885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually speaking of Heather, did any of the female users onthis site ever want a male Ghoul option in Bloodlines? I never thought of it before since I'm a guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't, but I did notice the lack of male options all around. I agree with what's already said, the issue with Heather is that she's sort of a waste of vitae. I never understood why other players got emotionally attached to her, but then again I tend to find ghouls too annoying and clingy to bother with, so.<br /> <br /> I guess Heather's just a symptom of the Fledgling's youth and lack of education. They don't fully grasp what they've done to her, what the point of a retainer is or how to manage one, and they're willing to waste valuable vitae on a sexy table lamp <s>that's not actually sexy at all and has no fashion sense.</s><br /> <br /> Poaching Mercurio would have been nice. Hell, even Nox. The game is combat heavy, so Yuki might've been useful, if only she'd stop with the gratuitous language mangling (also the whole &quot;should be in school&quot; issue, hampering her usefulness)<br /> <br /> As for Damsel, she has fans and she's entertaining to talk to even if I don't take her seriously. Going by Skelter's comments, you aren't supposed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-01-2021, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T02:05:08-07:00","id":1455913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455901#post1455901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted a useful ghoul with skills. Heather was a liability, and I resent the way sex appeal is misused in this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully admit that I like my vampire games dripping in sex.<br /> <br /> The big regret I have is the game didn't have something for female fans. Which is why La Croix, of all people, gets the most male fan art. Well Nines gets a little too.<br /> <br /> But yes, they should have thrown in some more male romances for the lady gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T02:14:58-07:00","id":1455915,"title":"","content":"I didn't understand the appeal of most pc/npc ships (especially Strauss), but I would pay for the sheer tragic hilarity of watching a dysfunctional romance with Lacroix explode horribly. Probably literally. The man is such a mess.<br /> <br /> Can't blame people making their own stuff though. If you want guys, you get very little in comparison. On the other hand, if you want girls you get... a little too much at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-01-2021, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T03:52:08-07:00","id":1455917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455913#post1455913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I fully admit that I like my vampire games dripping in sex.<br /> <br /> The big regret I have is the game didn't have something for female fans. Which is why La Croix, of all people, gets the most male fan art. Well Nines gets a little too.<br /> <br /> But yes, they should have thrown in some more male romances for the lady gamers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Me too, it helps me escape my cruel reality, but the stuff in VTMB was mostly very... adolescent fantasy, to put it diplomatically. It's barely passable given how VTMB doesn't take itself very seriously, but if VTMB was somewhat more serious... it'd be a red flag. I'm not a prude, but the context is just fucking awful.<br /> I totally have Vampires/Werewolves/mortal elite abuse their power for worldly indulgences, with crazy harems and shit, sometimes they view having sex with X and Y as a goal and view folks as trophies. But y'know, I don't act like that's a societally approved reward, where I think VTMB does. I want to work with VV because she grants me XP and maybe one day she can return a favour, not because... seemingly thirsty stripper who can't wind her neck in. You either go along with VV's BS or tell her to fuck off, you can't tell her to act like a normal fucking person. There are literally two fucking female characters in VTMB that aren't sex objects; a ghost, the nagaraja and the nosferatu, and the latter is mad that she's not a sex object anymore. Someone's got issues.<br /> <br /> (That said, the Deb of Night, wow. That's a voice. easily the hottest character)<br /> <br /> Just copy paste some meals around the clubs/bars. That's all ya need really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T04:08:38-07:00","id":1455919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455913#post1455913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, they should have thrown in some more male romances for the lady gamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone that wants some female-male and male-male romance options is a lady.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> Though I'm pretty sure we've already had a large and acrimonious thread about the sexism in VTMB's relationship options, presentations of female characters, and so on... which is getting away from anything Aveloone's blog post was actually about so... maybe lets move on from this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T04:15:15-07:00","id":1455920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455917#post1455917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> There are literally two fucking female characters in VTMB that aren't sex objects (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that too harsh on the game and the developers? Just because a character is sexualized doesn't mean that it is the main motif in regard to the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T04:52:37-07:00","id":1455923,"title":"","content":"Most all of the female vampires have sex appeal, but then vampires in general have sex appeal, especially in pop culture. The issue is that pretty much none of the guys have sex appeal. We needed some guys with sexuality too. If you had some balance between sexy girls and sexy guys I'd have less of an issue, but as all of the sex appeal was loaded almost entirely into the female characters, you ended up with a game that was almost entirely designed for the male gaze.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind though that personally my criticism is fairly light due to the fact that it's a 20 year old game, it's audience at the time very much was male gamers, and they <i>did</i> include some options throughout the game for female characters even if not nearly as many. That was fairly progressive for a game made during that time period (as an example Baldur's Gate 2 which had been released not long before had 3 romances available for male characters and only one available for female characters).<br /> <br /> These days, of course, we expect some level of equality in RPGs, but that wasn't really the case 20 years ago even though it should have always been something that game designers should have strived for. Ultimately Bloodlines could have been better in some areas, and in it was cringy in other areas (poster quest), but I think for what it was and for the time period it was made, I don't think it was all <i>that</i> egregious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T05:14:55-07:00","id":1455924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455923#post1455923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most all of the female vampires have sex appeal, but then vampires in general have sex appeal, especially in pop culture. The issue is that pretty much none of the guys have sex appeal. We needed some guys with sexuality too. If you had some balance between sexy girls and sexy guys I'd have less of an issue, but as all of the sex appeal was loaded almost entirely into the female characters, you ended up with a game that was almost entirely designed for the male gaze.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind though that personally my criticism is fairly light due to the fact that it's a 20 year old game, it's audience at the time very much was male gamers, and they <i>did</i> include some options throughout the game for female characters even if not nearly as many. That was fairly progressive for a game made during that time period (as an example Baldur's Gate 2 which had been released not long before had 3 romances available for male characters and only one available for female characters).<br /> <br /> These days, of course, we expect some level of equality in RPGs, but that wasn't really the case 20 years ago even though it should have always been something that game designers should have strived for. Ultimately Bloodlines could have been better in some areas, and in it was cringy in other areas (poster quest), but I think for what it was and for the time period it was made, I don't think it was all <i>that</i> egregious.</div> </div> </div> </div>What sorts of actions and appearance would you expect from VTMB characters to create an impression of 'sexy guys'? Surely it is not as simple as characters being shirtless. I guess flirting with a female PC would be a step in this direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T05:18:29-07:00","id":1455926,"title":"","content":"Setting up webcams in a woman's apartment so she can be publicly smeared and harassed to the point of suicide is pretty egregious even by 20 years ago standards; esp. when you can do it without any negative consequences by not taking the cash and thus avoiding a Humanity ding.<br /> <br /> Anyway.... can we... not retread this even more now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T05:48:26-07:00","id":1455930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455920#post1455920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that too harsh on the game and the developers? Just because a character is sexualized doesn't mean that it is the main motif in regard to the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. The game fully deserves the criticism. Even say, a character you can't romance, like the faux-japanese hunter, has horrible sexualized traits (the flailing skirt) <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455926#post1455926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting up webcams in a woman's apartment so she can be publicly smeared and harassed to the point of suicide is pretty egregious even by 20 years ago standards; esp. when you can do it without any negative consequences by not taking the cash and thus avoiding a Humanity ding.<br /> <br /> Anyway.... can we... not retread this even more now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly disagree. Other than the humanity/cash issue (and the part where the player should do missions for XP above all things) this mission is fine. The nosferatu tells you exactly what she wants you to do. The malice is clearly stated and there is no deception or illusion that this is a noble act (bar perhaps hiding how fragile the victim's mental state is). You are free to refuse the mission. You're even free to bully the quest giver. This is... normal amoral vampire behaviour, and you, a human, are expected to feel guilt from it. There's not much wrong with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T06:20:22-07:00","id":1455931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455913#post1455913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I fully admit that I like my vampire games dripping in sex.<br /> <br /> The big regret I have is the game didn't have something for female fans. Which is why La Croix, of all people, gets the most male fan art. Well Nines gets a little too.<br /> <br /> But yes, they should have thrown in some more male romances for the lady gamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, VTMB simply isn't a sexy game. That's okay. There are lots of good games that aren't sexy. But most of them don't have a seduction as a mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455924#post1455924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sorts of actions and appearance would you expect from VTMB characters to create an impression of 'sexy guys'? Surely it is not as simple as characters being shirtless. I guess flirting with a female PC would be a step in this direction?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Plenty of men in the game are physically good looking, but none of the male vampires express any sexuality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455909#post1455909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Damsel, she has fans and she's entertaining to talk to even if I don't take her seriously. Going by Skelter's comments, you aren't supposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>As if we're supposed to take the opinion of a Vietnam War apologist more seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T11:13:22-07:00","id":1455942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455915#post1455915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't understand the appeal of most pc/npc ships (especially Strauss), but I would pay for the sheer tragic hilarity of watching a dysfunctional romance with Lacroix explode horribly. Probably literally. The man is such a mess.<br /> <br /> Can't blame people making their own stuff though. If you want guys, you get very little in comparison. On the other hand, if you want girls you get... a little too much at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't see romances as anything inherently different from combat or politics. Romances are an intrinsic part of the human experience and thus storytelling as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455917#post1455917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me too, it helps me escape my cruel reality, but the stuff in VTMB was mostly very... adolescent fantasy, to put it diplomatically. It's barely passable given how VTMB doesn't take itself very seriously, but if VTMB was somewhat more serious... it'd be a red flag. I'm not a prude, but the context is just fucking awful.<br /> <br /> I totally have Vampires/Werewolves/mortal elite abuse their power for worldly indulgences, with crazy harems and shit, sometimes they view having sex with X and Y as a goal and view folks as trophies. But y'know, I don't act like that's a societally approved reward, where I think VTMB does. I want to work with VV because she grants me XP and maybe one day she can return a favour, not because... seemingly thirsty stripper who can't wind her neck in. You either go along with VV's BS or tell her to fuck off, you can't tell her to act like a normal fucking person. There are literally two fucking female characters in VTMB that aren't sex objects; a ghost, the nagaraja and the nosferatu, and the latter is mad that she's not a sex object anymore. Someone's got issues.<br /> <br /> (That said, the Deb of Night, wow. That's a voice. easily the hottest character)<br /> <br /> Just copy paste some meals around the clubs/bars. That's all ya need really.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is that I think the Mods to VV's quest are one of the few times they make it worse because a lot of gamers are like, &quot;Wait a second, she's just leaving me high and dry now?&quot; Yes, OF COURSE she is. After VV gets what she wants from you, she has no further use for her. She's a TOREADOR. The lack of &quot;follow up&quot; is deliberate.<br /> <br /> She's a stripper as her profession because it suits Toreador manipulation. They provide the illusion of sex and enticement but, at the end of the day, it's all a performance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455926#post1455926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting up webcams in a woman's apartment so she can be publicly smeared and harassed to the point of suicide is pretty egregious even by 20 years ago standards; esp. when you can do it without any negative consequences by not taking the cash and thus avoiding a Humanity ding.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a notable thing because there's so few examples of being able to be genuinely evil in the game that it stands out way more than it might normally. I'm not against some evil quests in the game but I would have felt much better about it if you'd had the option of warning Tawni at the expense of a Masquerade point or something similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway.... can we... not retread this even more now? </div> </div> </div>I dunno, discussing sex and sexuality in Vampire as well as gaming isn't an inherently bad topic for a horror game. Nor is it off topic that much since it relates to Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> It seems valid as long as people stay respectful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-01-2021, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T12:02:47-07:00","id":1455944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455942#post1455942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I don't see romances as anything inherently different from combat or politics. Romances are an intrinsic part of the human experience and thus storytelling as a whole.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not against romance subplots. They can certainly add to the story, like in Night Road where it's all fun and games suppressing your survival instincts and common sense in order to hit on the two-centuries-old prince until it turns out you ate his girlfriend's soul. (Oops?)<br /> <br /> The bloodlines cast just hold no appeal to me, personally, for some reason. Though I'll admit whether VV genuinely likes you on some level is interesting to ponder, she's still rather... Empty. Fitting for a Toreador, perhaps, but not terribly good at holding the attention.<br /> Similarly, sexual themes/content isn't something I consider a problem. Bloodlines just feels a touch oversaturated with it.<br /> <br /> Wasn't there talk of Bloodlines 2 having romances? I wonder how that was meant to/will go...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-01-2021, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T13:12:43-07:00","id":1455947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455944#post1455944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I'm not against romance subplots. They can certainly add to the story, like in Night Roads where it's all fun and games suppressing your survival instincts and common sense in order to hit on the two-centuries-old prince until it turns out you ate his girlfriend's soul. (Oops?)<br /> <br /> The bloodlines cast just hold no appeal to me, personally, for some reason. Though I'll admit whether VV genuinely likes you on some level is interesting to ponder, she's still rather... Empty. Fitting for a Toreador, perhaps, but not terribly good at holding the attention.<br /> Similarly, sexual themes/content isn't something I consider a problem. Bloodlines just feels a touch oversaturated with it.<br /> <br /> Wasn't there talk of Bloodlines 2 having romances? I wonder how that was meant to/will go...</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily, that was one of the constant questions asked of the staff of the game and they never answered it.<br /> <br /> Which to me suggests that, no, there weren't any romances in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T13:40:19-07:00","id":1455949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455930#post1455930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than the humanity/cash issue (and the part where the player should do missions for XP above all things) this mission is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Humanity issue... is the issue. You can help bully someone to the point of suicide, and no matter what you get XP out of it, despite knowing exactly what you're doing, and you <b>benefit from it mechanically</b>. One of the larger problems with BL1 is how weakly Humanity is enforced. Model Citizen is an obviously evil side-quest, but you get to completely skip the &quot;consequences of being evil&quot; meter by not taking cash for the job. &quot;It's not evil to break multiple laws for the express purpose of ruining a woman's career to such an extent that she kills herself from the public trauma, it's only evil if you take money for it,&quot; is an epic bad take. What's wrong with it is that the game doesn't give you any reason to (a) refuse the quest because XP and (b) feel guilty about it as the player.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're even free to bully the quest giver. </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you want to give up on the XP, or spend a net $200 on another side quest to get the XP granting side quest back as an option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455942#post1455942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a notable thing because there's so few examples of being able to be genuinely evil in the game that it stands out way more than it might normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I think you're confusing, &quot;so few examples of being able to genuinely risk losing Humanity in the game,&quot; with examples of doing things most people would consider morally repugnant.<br /> <br /> The whole reason Humanity is a joke in BL1 is because, as Jack lays out in the opening, it only applies to innocents (and even that is very poorly applied). The game basically encourages you to be Dexter Morgan: be a sociopath that targets criminals. That way you can easily end the game with Humanity 8-10 despite a body count of humans that would put you in the record books and get all the sweet sweet XP to actually beat the game instead of skipping out on all the XP if you want to actually play a somewhat moral character.<br /> <br /> The beginning main quest line is to get a powerful explosive, and then use it on a building full of living people.<br /> <br /> The most optimal way of dealing with Dennis and his thugs is killing them because on top of the XP/cash rewards sneaking gets (social gets the worst rewards) you can get a bunch of starter weapons for free and sell the ones you don't use to Trip for more cash.<br /> <br /> When you blow up the warehouse, stealth is actually the optimal path, but that means you still end up blowing up a ton of people. But that's OK, gang members working for the Sabbat don't count as people any more. Nevermind that one bum can kill (causing Humanity loss if you kill him to make sure he doesn't make noise) who's going to get blown up too since apparently killing him is wrong.. if you do it directly instead of with the boom.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but killing around three dozen humans in two acts of gang turf warfare (you're not even killing them as a vigilante or some appeal to that sort of thinking) is pretty evil. But the only Humanity loss is if you murder the homeless guy directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not against some evil quests in the game but I would have felt much better about it if you'd had the option of warning Tawni at the expense of a Masquerade point or something similar. </div> </div> </div>Or if the Humanity loss wasn't avoidable. Or if you didn't get XP for it. There's no point in evil quests in a game with a morality meter if you can skip the morality meter while still benefiting from doing the evil quest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno, discussing sex and sexuality in Vampire as well as gaming isn't an inherently bad topic for a horror game. Nor is it off topic that much since it relates to Bloodlines. </div> </div> </div>It's a request to the posters in the thread considering how poorly the 21 page thread on sexism in BL1 went. I'm not asking you, as a mod, to force it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T14:09:00-07:00","id":1455953,"title":"","content":"Humanity <i>is</i> far too easy to achieve and too hard to lose, evident in the fact that you can get the impossible rating of 10. <br /> Bloodline's humanity doesn't really follow the hierarchy of sins, does it? I don't remember losing humanity for stealing things. So it's sort of screwy from the get go. Killing in self-defence is unplanned, but still killing. <br /> If VtMB used it, the Fledgling would have a rating of 3-2. 1, if you were really trying to be an asshole. Is there anything you can do in game that qualifies as a humanity 1 violation?<br /> <br /> To get high humanity, you'd need to run around pursued by mobs of enemies all the time. Or rely on stealth and/or socialising.<br /> <br /> Huh. I'm tempted to assign the pc virtues and replay the game while rolling conscience and manually editing humanity. I wonder what the results would be...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-01-2021, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T16:07:15-07:00","id":1455967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455953#post1455953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity <i>is</i> far too easy to achieve and too hard to lose, evident in the fact that you can get the impossible rating of 10.<br /> Bloodline's humanity doesn't really follow the hierarchy of sins, does it? I don't remember losing humanity for stealing things. So it's sort of screwy from the get go. Killing in self-defence is unplanned, but still killing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, it does seem to be more 5th Edition than Revised and may actually be what inspired 5th Edition.<br /> <br /> Don't Kill Innocents allows you to do an action-horror game like the game is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If VtMB used it, the Fledgling would have a rating of 3-2. 1, if you were really trying to be an asshole. Is there anything you can do in game that qualifies as a humanity 1 violation? </div> </div> </div>Diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-01-2021, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T19:12:32-07:00","id":1455981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455953#post1455953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity <i>is</i> far too easy to achieve and too hard to lose, evident in the fact that you can get the impossible rating of 10.<br /> Bloodline's humanity doesn't really follow the hierarchy of sins, does it? I don't remember losing humanity for stealing things. So it's sort of screwy from the get go. Killing in self-defence is unplanned, but still killing.<br /> If VtMB used it, the Fledgling would have a rating of 3-2. 1, if you were really trying to be an asshole. Is there anything you can do in game that qualifies as a humanity 1 violation?<br /> <br /> To get high humanity, you'd need to run around pursued by mobs of enemies all the time. Or rely on stealth and/or socialising.<br /> <br /> Huh. I'm tempted to assign the pc virtues and replay the game while rolling conscience and manually editing humanity. I wonder what the results would be...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bloodlines was loosely based on VtM mechanics, as loosely as they needed to make the style of game they had work. So Humanity wasn't based on the old sins lists, Dominate and Dementation and Protean and others did different things than in TT. It's just part of the transition to vidya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T19:20:41-07:00","id":1455984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455942#post1455942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, discussing sex and sexuality in Vampire as well as gaming isn't an inherently bad topic for a horror game. Nor is it off topic that much since it relates to Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it doesn't really have anything to do with Avellone's statement.<br /> <br /> Probably should be spun off into its own thread, or just make a general Bloodlines 2 thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T02:17:27-07:00","id":1455996,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines was wonky in a lot of ways and had so many game breaking bugs at release the company basically went bankrupt.<br /> <br /> They attempted to &quot;game-ify&quot; Humanity but, as pointed out, there are lots of places where it falls flat. I imagine if the game had had a more reasonable development process with proper beta testing and follow up patches various issues with Humanity might have been fixed or implemented a bit better.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I'd chalk up problems with Humanity more to the poor development process rather than any sort of active maliciousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T04:13:12-07:00","id":1456000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455996#post1455996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines was wonky in a lot of ways and had so many game breaking bugs at release the company basically went bankrupt.<br /> <br /> <b>They attempted to &quot;game-ify&quot; Humanity but, as pointed out, there are lots of places where it falls flat. I imagine if the game had had a more reasonable development process with proper beta testing and follow up patches various issues with Humanity might have been fixed or implemented a bit better.</b><br /> <br /> Ultimately I'd chalk up problems with Humanity more to the poor development process rather than any sort of active maliciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game has twenty years of development since and we have a great fanbase devoted to it as is.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can change how it handles humanity and killing without changing the nature of the game as an action RPG.<br /> <br /> And to be honest, I feel like the game would be less enjoyable if you couldn't kill as many people as you do. Fidelity to the tabletop would have made it worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-02-2021, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T07:21:57-07:00","id":1456007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1456000#post1456000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game has twenty years of development since and we have a great fanbase devoted to it as is.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can change how it handles humanity and killing without changing the nature of the game as an action RPG.<br /> <br /> And to be honest, I feel like the game would be less enjoyable if you couldn't kill as many people as you do. Fidelity to the tabletop would have made it worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, finding creative ways to do what you need to do to survive in kinded society while avoiding humanity loss is one of the appeals of aiming for a high rating on the path of humanity, and it would've been interesting to see that in game. I do prefer V5's flexible tents+convictions approach to humanity though, so I'm not torn up about VtMB's, uh, flippancy(?), even if it did feel a bit shallow in play, like in Imalia's quest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Diablerie </div> </div> </div>Is there anyone worth diablerising? The Voerman twins are 6th gen, so maybe...<br /> Oh, and Lacroix is also higher gen, since he can dominate the PC. Don't know how much higher though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-02-2021, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T11:05:47-07:00","id":1456017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455967#post1455967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't Kill Innocents allows you to do an action-horror game like the game is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problems arise with all the innocents you can get away with killing that aren't a threat to your Humanity anyway, the very dubious ways the game defines &quot;innocents,&quot; and the ease of gaining Humanity as a quest reward compared to losing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Diablerie. </div> </div> </div>There's no diablerie in the game, that's something that's only possible in some of the mods that add significant content to the game (instead of things like the Unofficial Patch which cleans up bugs and restores content).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1456000#post1456000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can change how it handles humanity and killing without changing the nature of the game as an action RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that really so bad though? One of the consistent complaints about the game is how it makes it seem like stealh and social are viable paths through the game, but you really only need them for some side-quests and optimizing your XP gains, while combat is the most important part of the game to focus on as the game progresses and combat becomes more and more mandatory.<br /> <br /> A stronger Humanity system could easily help make it feel less like picking non-combat focus is a dumb choice, as it would turn the combat-focused style into a much more &quot;high risk, high reward,&quot; approach if just murdering your way through the game would most likely cause a lose condition of Humanity loss instead of being the easy way to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to be honest, I feel like the game would be less enjoyable if you couldn't kill as many people as you do. Fidelity to the tabletop would have made it worse. </div> </div> </div>Lots of games have managed a better balance of these things... so that makes this feel very uncompelling. BL1's failings might be easy to get over due to the limitations of budgets and time, but that doesn't mean the game was up against some sort of wall of what was capable of being done in gaming at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455981#post1455981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines was loosely based on VtM mechanics, as loosely as they needed to make the style of game they had work. So Humanity wasn't based on the old sins lists, Dominate and Dementation and Protean and others did different things than in TT. It's just part of the transition to vidya.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. BL 1 still fails to enforce it's own definitions of Humanity in a meaningful way. As I noted above, there's an NPC you get a Humanity knock if you just kill him while he's standing around, but if you leave him there to die when you blow up the building he's standing near, you don't. This sort of loophole permeates the game as things the game acknowledges should dock you Humanity are granted workarounds so you don't lose from your Humanity dropping (even though that's supposed to be a risk)..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1455996#post1455996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately I'd chalk up problems with Humanity more to the poor development process rather than any sort of active maliciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I call out things like Model Citizen or Poster Quest, it's not about any sort of judgement on whether or not the creators were being actively malicious. Just that (1) they're examples of some pretty ugly writing in the game and (2) they were still creepy things to do the way they were done 20 years ago; changing norms doesn't defend the choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T11:33:58-07:00","id":1456020,"title":"","content":"If you want to do a game about slaughtering Inquisitors, Kuei-Jin, and crooks then a harsher Humanity system would make that a problem, though. Especially if you are otherwise playing a good guy.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think that it isn't necessarily a bad thing to have a looser combat system if you want players to fight monsters and have fun doing it.<br /> <br /> Its why VAMPYR only punishes you if you murder citizens versus drinking from Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T11:41:30-07:00","id":1456021,"title":"","content":"Please cite for me any time Bloodlines (either of them) has been sold as a game about slaughtering things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T14:01:19-07:00","id":1456033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1456021#post1456021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please cite for me any time Bloodlines (either of them) has been sold as a game about slaughtering things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an action RPG.<br /> <br /> I'm confused at what the problem is. I love action scenes. Being a vampire going hog wild on the Sabbat with a flame thrower, getting into fights with my katana, and the battle against La Croix's minions.<br /> <br /> I love the Visual Novels but part of the fun of Bloodlines is the battles. Certainly, I don't see why the game would be richer without them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T14:47:06-07:00","id":1456038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1456033#post1456033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an action RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>What it is, and what it's sold as, are two different things; which is a problem.<br /> <br /> All of the things the game says are valid things to pursue, but aren't because they're not really action RPG things to do, don't mesh well with the idea that it's just supposed to be an action RPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm confused at what the problem is. </div> </div> </div>As seems to frequently be a source of confusion for you, different people can love the same game for different reasons, and those differences in reasons results in different issues with how the game lives up to their expectations. We both love VtM, but you love V5, and I'm massively disappointed with it to the point of never wanting to play it. Because we have different perspectives and different wants out of a VtM TTRPG, just as we seem to have different wants out of a VtM cRPG. I confused that this is still something I have to explain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love action scenes. Being a vampire going hog wild on the Sabbat with a flame thrower, getting into fights with my katana, and the battle against La Croix's minions. </div> </div> </div>I love action scenes... I find them one of BL1's weakest aspects but something you have to engage with because the game gets more and more combat-mandatory as time goes on. BL1's combat scenes are generally tedious and boring as you face 2-3 repeated foes on repetitive maps with no effort at all into trying to add a sense of variety to the action via terrain and placement. The boss fights are generally just hard enough the casual players (esp. when deal with the janky physics) will get frustrated by them, but not challenging once more dedicated players figure out the one (and generally only one) way to beat them (which is generally also pretty tedious), making your losses feel cheap and your victories feel hollow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certainly, I don't see why the game would be richer without them. </div> </div> </div>Nobody said anything of the sort. You keep deflecting criticism of the game with these strawmen.<br /> <br /> The game would be richer by utilizing its existing Humanity mechanics to make the game less of a power fantasy and more true to the World of Darkness by having you either really struggle with Humanity if you're going to mow down every obstacle in your path, or force you to be more judicious in your use of violence so you can unleash when you need to, but not overdo it and fall to the Beast.<br /> <br /> The game would also be richer if levels like Grout's Mansion, the fight to get to the Warrens, the parking garage side quest for Fat Larry, and the plaguebearer cult house weren't tedious slogs. Even the better designed levels like the attack on the SoL base are too long for the combat system even if there's some good options besides &quot;shoot everything before it shoots you.&quot; It's not a matter of getting rid of the action, but executing it better (and doing level design so there's more options for stealth and social builds).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T19:17:41-07:00","id":1456048,"title":"","content":"I disagree, I think it's fine as a Power Fantasy and more fun this way. But it's a matter of taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T21:41:07-07:00","id":1456053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1456033#post1456033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I love the Visual Novels but part of the fun of Bloodlines is the battles. Certainly, I don't see why the game would be richer without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally had more fun when i could use my powers with the dialogue system and avoid combat with conversation.<br /> <br /> Edit: One little detail, its less Visual Novel and more adventure game ala Monkey Island or Dreamfall: The longest journey","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 08-03-2021, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T01:54:38-07:00","id":1456061,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed the flexibility of the earlier game. It was a very different experience to play as a social butterfly Tremere, vs a high humanity Malk who avoids socialisation like the plague and sticks to obfuscate and hacking, and finally a low humanity Nossie who put every discipline dot into potence and revelled in slaughtering her way through every location.<br /> <br /> It added to roleplay, and made the game more immersive and replayable to have options. (It was also hilarious stumbling into the occasional boss fight and trying to survive then with characters unsuited for combat.) But by the end, all playstyles tapered out into fighting, and I wouldn't consider that a plus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-03-2021, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T04:15:28-07:00","id":1456066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455130-chris-avellone-finally-explains-what-the-hell-happened-with-bloodlines-2?p=1456048#post1456048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, I think it's fine as a Power Fantasy and more fun this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem: it's actually a bad action RPG. It's a good RPG with poorly implemented action/stealth mechanics.<br /> <br /> You don't have to go take my opinion on this, you can just search any of dozens of ranking websites that aggregate reviews. Even positive reviews tend to count the combat and action as the low points in the game (after the bugs).<br /> <br /> Why is it a beloved cult classic game?<br /> <br /> Atmosphere, writing, and world building. If you just want power fantasy, there are literally hundreds of better games out there, and dozens if you require an RPG element to them. What makes it special is that it does such a fantastic job of communicating the gothic-punk concept of the WoD, and the dark, sleazy, grim infested nature of Vampire.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of positive reviews of the game fall into that conclusion: combat is something you put up with because the rest of the game is so evocative and fun that the action and bugs and other issues are worth tolerating for how great the game does at making you feel what &quot;our world but darker&quot; really means.<br /> <br /> We can't actually discuss this stuff if you're going to retreat into &quot;well I like it.&quot; That's not a discussion, that's just people speaking opinions at each other. What do you think is actually good about BL1 as power fantasy action RPG? What does it do right? Why is it better than other games in the subgenre?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it's a matter of taste. </div> </div> </div>Which is a cop out. I point out why I have my opinions on the game with examples and explanations. Tell us why all the zombies you have to get past before Bishop Vick are actually fun to deal with. After the first dozen of them, what do they add compared to the time it takes to deal with them?<br /> <br /> Just because it's subjective doesn't mean you can't actually talk about the game for what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T10:19:50-07:00","id":1463236,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.belloflostsouls.net/2021/10/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-still-in-development-despite-cancellations.html\" target=\"_blank\">In related news, <i>Bloodlines II </i>is supposedly not canceled according to an article at BoLS.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>From the article</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Publisher Paradox Interactive recently made an announcement stating that they had canceled many \u201cunannounced projects\u201d in order to refocus their efforts on \u201cproven game niches.\u201d What exactly that means is anyone\u2019s guess, but Paradox went on to clarify that in spite of all this, the beleaguered <i>Bloodlines 2</i> was still in development\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I am taking all of this with a grain of salt, and will continue to do so until I hear more about at least hiring a new creative director, and the game becoming something of a priority for the companies involved.<br /> <br /> But it seemed worthwhile to share the news here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T10:39:30-07:00","id":1463239,"title":"","content":"It is good that you shared the news. There is still hope for <i>VtM: Bloodlines 2</i>...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/4/4d/Elif_in_trailer1.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20200507174001\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/4/4d/Elif_in_trailer1.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20200507174001\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/4/4d/Elif_in_trailer1.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20200507174001\" target=\"_blank\"> https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/4/4d/Elif_in_trailer1.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20200507174001 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-13-2021, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}